Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Parts Buffer
Select the Parts Buffer. This is the object into which the Worker deposits the parts he could not deliver,
when he walks back to the WorkerPool at the end of his shift.
Remarks
Click the ellipsis button and select the Parts Buffer in the dialog Select Object.
You can also drag a material flow object onto the image of the WorkerPool in your model Frame and drop
it there to use it as the Parts Buffer.
The Parts Buffer can be any one of the material flow objects, which accepts parts. If you did not assign a
parts buffer to the WorkerPool, and a Worker arrives with parts at the end of its shift in the WorkerPool,
Plant Simulation shows a warning and stops the simulation.
If you activated the transport importer of the Parts Buffer, one of the available Workers carries the parts
in the Parts Buffer to the destination object, after the next shift has started. If you did not activate the
transport importer, the parts in the Parts Buffer are moved on according to the Exit Strategy which you
selected for the Parts Buffer.
Note
This setting only applies, when you control the shifts worked in your facility with the Shift Calendar
[WorkerPool].
